{"data": [{"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:43:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118761242340868359"], "id": "2118761242340868359", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 26, "impression_count": 14469, "like_count": 89, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 26}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118756628388348345", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The PRC side has been playing Trump, Bessent and Greer for chumps over the rare earths deal. The frustration has been under-appreciated, why I wrote Wednesday \"One thing to consider is that the Trump Administration held back on some actions on China because of concerns of the PRC https://t.co/ZOyW5ZJFOz", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2118761242340868359"}, {"author_id": "961132338", "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:28:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118757377491296365"], "id": "2118757377491296365", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 3314, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Turns out one of the best assets for hedging AI slowdown risk is...French government bonds\n\nhttps://t.co/X09aQENTIs\n\n(I half-jokingly pitched this to @rbrtrmstrng weeks ago, should have had more conviction)", "url": "https://x.com/M_C_Klein/status/2118757377491296365"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:17:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118754660567957752"], "id": "2118754660567957752", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 22, "impression_count": 34100, "like_count": 408, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 27, "retweet_count": 6}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118542240733888791", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Feels like we might be, for the first time, seeing a shift away from prioritizing Boomers in our politics. It’s Gen X’s turn now. https://t.co/GzKgEWzPb7", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2118754660567957752"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:06:52.000Z", "edit_